2️⃣ DBT Project Structure

When you run dbt init, you get a project like:

dbt_project.yml
models/
   staging/
   marts/
   core/
seeds/
tests/
macros/


models/ → SQL files that define transformations.

seeds/ → CSV files that can be loaded as tables.

tests/ → data quality checks.

macros/ → reusable SQL logic with Jinja.

dbt_project.yml → configuration file.

3️⃣ Models

A model is just a .sql file in the models/ folder.

🔹 Example: models/staging/stg_customers.sql

{{ config(materialized='view') }}

SELECT
    id AS customer_id,
    name,
    email,
    created_at
FROM raw.customers;


👉 Run:

dbt run --select stg_customers


This will create a view in Snowflake.

4️⃣ Materializations

Defines how DBT builds the model.
Options: view, table, incremental, ephemeral.

(a) View
{{ config(materialized='view') }}
SELECT * FROM raw.customers;

(b) Table
{{ config(materialized='table') }}
SELECT * FROM raw.orders;

(c) Incremental

Good for large tables (only new data is added).

{{ config(
    materialized='incremental',
    unique_key='order_id'
) }}

SELECT *
FROM raw.orders
{% if is_incremental() %}
  WHERE updated_at > (SELECT MAX(updated_at) FROM {{ this }})
{% endif %}

(d) Ephemeral

Used only in DBT compile, not in warehouse.

{{ config(materialized='ephemeral') }}
SELECT * FROM raw.temp_data;

5️⃣ Sources

Define external tables as sources in schema.yml.

version: 2

sources:
  - name: raw
    schema: raw
    tables:
      - name: customers
      - name: orders


Then use in SQL:

SELECT * FROM {{ source('raw', 'customers') }}

6️⃣ Seeds

CSV files that DBT loads into warehouse.

🔹 Example:
seeds/country_codes.csv

country_code,country_name
IN,India
US,United States


Load it:

dbt seed


Then query:

SELECT * FROM {{ ref('country_codes') }}

7️⃣ Tests

Used for data quality.

Built-in Tests

In schema.yml:

models:
  - name: stg_customers
    columns:
      - name: customer_id
        tests:
          - not_null
          - unique


Run:

dbt test

Custom Test

tests/positive_amount.sql

SELECT *
FROM {{ ref('stg_orders') }}
WHERE amount < 0

8️⃣ Documentation

DBT auto-generates docs.

models:
  - name: stg_customers
    description: "Staging model for customers"
    columns:
      - name: customer_id
        description: "Unique ID for customers"


Build docs:

dbt docs generate
dbt docs serve

9️⃣ Jinja & Macros

DBT uses Jinja templating.

🔹 Example Macro: macros/get_country.sql

{% macro get_country_name(code) %}
    CASE
        WHEN {{ code }} = 'IN' THEN 'India'
        WHEN {{ code }} = 'US' THEN 'United States'
        ELSE 'Unknown'
    END
{% endmacro %}


Use in model:

SELECT
    id,
    {{ get_country_name('country_code') }} AS country
FROM raw.customers;

🔟 Hooks & Operations

Run SQL before/after model build.

{{ config(
    materialized='table',
    pre_hook="DELETE FROM audit_log WHERE model='orders'",
    post_hook="INSERT INTO audit_log VALUES('orders', current_timestamp)"
) }}

SELECT * FROM raw.orders;

1️⃣1️⃣ Snapshots

Used to track historical changes (SCD Type 2).

snapshots/customer_snapshot.sql

{% snapshot customer_snapshot %}
{{ config(
    target_schema='snapshots',
    unique_key='customer_id',
    strategy='timestamp',
    updated_at='updated_at'
) }}

SELECT * FROM raw.customers;
{% endsnapshot %}


Run:

dbt snapshot

1️⃣2️⃣ Deployment Flow (Real-Time)

dev branch → developers build new models.

test branch → QA validates models.

main branch → production-ready models.

CI/CD (GitHub Actions, dbt Cloud, or Airflow) deploys automatically.

✅ Summary of DBT Concepts

Models → SQL transformations

Materializations → View, Table, Incremental, Ephemeral

Sources → raw data mapping

Seeds → load CSV files

Tests → data quality

Documentation → docs site

Jinja/Macros → reusable SQL

Hooks → pre/post SQL actions

Snapshots → historical tracking
🔟 Deployment → CI/CD